  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "A common departure from normality is positive skewness, such that the tail to the right of the mean is longer than that to the left. Such a pattern is often indicative of a log-normal distribution, in which case a simple logarithmic transformation gives a normal distribution (Figure 11.1).",
